title {title}
' Trust-zone classes (in the style block above): <<zone-untrusted>> <<zone-dmz>> <<zone-internal>> <<zone-restricted>> <<zone-external>>
' Network recipe: zones are rectangles with a <<zone-...>> class and the CIDR on a second line;
' the firewall is the <<accent>>; edges carry protocol/port only; flows go INTO ZONES (link the
' rectangle, not its members) unless the member matters. Keep nesting to zone > device.
' HA pairs: one rectangle "FW pair (HA)" holding both nodes, joined with a plain  fwa - fwb  (no label).
' External clouds (M365, SaaS) go on their own rank, never inside the DMZ row. Split big networks by
' layer (physical / logical VLAN / policy) or by site, with <<muted>> "(see X)" stub nodes.

cloud "Internet" as inet <<zone-untrusted>>
